@startuml
' What: what a most / least mark does to the line and to the profile (D-32, D-34, D-35, D-44).
' Shows: the line effect (change, hold, dice) and the profile signal (ego up or down) of each kind of mark,
'        including the same-line cancel of D-35 ("inner turn").
' Source: brainstorming-base.md, D-32, D-34, D-35, D-44.
title Effects of a mark on the line and the profile
start
:Player marks a trembling line;
if (most and least on the same line?) then (yes)
  :Line: treated as unmarked, the dice decide;
  if (most = fitting and least = tempting?) then (yes)
    :Ego down twice ("inner turn");
  else (no)
    :Ego up twice;
  endif
elseif (most?) then (yes)
  :Line changes;
  :Sets an era policy (D-44);
elseif (least?) then (yes)
  :Line is held;
  :No new policy;
else (unmarked)
  :The dice decide;
  :No policy, no profile signal;
endif
:Profile signal of single marks:\nmost fitting or least tempting -> ego down\nmost tempting or least fitting -> ego up\ntempting matching own temperament -> temperament hardens;
stop
@enduml
